# Negative controls for the important-gates step (plan 04-24, D-46, RUN-04): a registry id that no
# inventory of its mechanism lists, and a Phase 4 requirement without a registry line.
important-gates-unknown-id
important-gates-uncovered-gate
# Plan 05-12 (RUN-04 extended): a Phase 5 requirement without a registry line, a Phase 5 line naming an unknown id,
# and a line naming a Phase 5 requirement outside the six.
important-gates-req-uncovered-phase5
important-gates-unknown-id-phase5
important-gates-bad-req-phase5
# Plan 06-14 (RUN-04 extended): a Phase 6 requirement without a registry line, a Phase 6 line naming an unknown id,
# and a line naming a Phase 6 requirement outside the five (VID-05 belongs to Phase 8).
important-gates-req-uncovered-phase6
important-gates-unknown-id-phase6
important-gates-bad-req-phase6
# Plan 07-02 (A-13, A-21): SCN-01 accepted; a Phase 7 requirement without a registry line.
important-gates-req-uncovered-phase7
# Plan 09-05 (EV-04, A-01): the derived must-be-covered set, both directions. A Complete requirement
# with no registry line and no exclusion (important-gates-complete-uncovered) and an exclusion whose
# requirement is not Complete (important-gates-excluded-stale), in one run. The FORBID names
# important-gates-unknown-id only: a Complete-and-unregistered requirement also trips the generic
# important-gates-uncovered-gate, so forbidding that token would make the control unsatisfiable.
important-gates-complete-uncovered
